From: pVisor <pvisor@local>
Subject: fuse: keep a guest directory image and deferred read-only opens

Negotiate FUSE_PVISOR_META and import directory metadata in paged,
variable-sized READINDEX replies up to 1 MiB. ENOSYS disables the image
for that directory, allowing mutable backings to retain ordinary FUSE
lookup and readdir semantics. Zero-validity one-shot names remain host
lookups and are hidden from readdir. Directory images own no dentries.

Defer regular-file OPEN until I/O, retaining original credentials and
binding outstanding opens before unlink, rename, copy-up, or attribute changes.
Serialize binding with release, honor the host's cache flags, and keep
SEEK_SET/CUR/END local while metadata is valid. Refreshed attributes use
an inode query until the file has a real host handle.

